# Synopsis

Manage session hooks: shell scripts that run when the chat session enters or
leaves a state.

# Operations

- "create": create a hook. Requires "state" and "source". "mode" selects how
  the hook content is provided: "command" (source is the shell script text),
  "copy" (source is a file whose content is copied), "symlink" (source is a
  file the hook links to). "name" is optional; an auto-generated name is used
  when omitted. "append" requires "name" and appends to the existing hook
  instead of failing; it can not be used with mode "symlink". "type"
  ("oneshot" runs once then is removed, "always" runs every time) defaults to
  "oneshot"; "when" ("before" entering / "after" leaving the state) defaults
  to "after".
- "remove": remove a hook. Requires "state" and "name".
- "list": list existing hooks. "state", "type" and "when" can be used to
  filter the list.
- "path": print the absolute pathname of a hook. Requires "state" and "name".

# States

any-state, read-loop, agent-loop-api-call, agent-loop-tool-call,
agent-loop-end, agent-loop-api-call-interrupted,
agent-loop-tool-call-interrupted, end.

# Approval

"create" and "remove" require approval on the controlling terminal. In
non-interactive sessions they are rejected unless automatic approval is
configured.

# Returns

A JSON object. On success: create returns
{"created":"<rel>","path":...} ({"appended":"<rel>","path":...} when
appending); remove returns {"removed":"<rel>","path":...}; list returns
{"hooks":[{"rel":...,"path":...},...]}; path returns {"path":...}.
On failure: {"error": <reason>}; when rejected: {"rejected": <reason>}.

<rel> is the relative hook path in the form state/type/when/name.

# Notes

Use this tool to install scripts that run automatically on session state
changes (for example desktop notifications or log appends), not to run
commands directly; use the shell tool for that.
